From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 02:45:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 106/121] spec: rejection sampling with a reduced (hot) draft
 vocab

Scatter every draft proposal q into the target vocab (zero off the hot set)
instead of refusing --speculative-use-rejection-sampling when a token map is
set. q is truncated like the verify truncates p (top-k cap 64, then the
request's top-k/top-p; SGLANG_RS_DRAFT_TOPK=0 keeps the untruncated q), which
keeps greedy requests on the argmax chain and raises sum(min(p, q)). The draft
graph now reads per-request top-k/top-p buffers; the RS draft-extend records
the C1 position-0 confidence like the greedy path. Draft rows are written in
place into one (bs, steps, vocab) tensor instead of a per-step stack.

Offline check (Triton interpreter, 20k rows/case): emitted-token distributions
match p at every chain position (chi2), greedy reproduces the target argmax.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
